data: {"type": "final", "payload": "## 核查结论：部分支持\n\n**\"检索增强生成（RAG）能够降低大语言模型的幻觉风险\"这一论断，在文献库中属于\"部分支持\"——即方向上有证据支持，但并非绝对成立，且存在反例。**\n\n**支持的一面（3 条证据）**\n\n- 《Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2023) 明确指出 RAG 是\"缓解大语言模型幻觉的有前景方法\"（promising approach for mitigating hallucination），这是对论断最直接的正面支持。\n- 《ReRag: A New Architecture for Reducing the Hallucination by Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2024) 表明 RAG 系统正是为应对幻觉问题而被引入的，其标题本身即指向\"降低幻觉\"这一目标。\n- 另有证据从\"解决知识截止问题\"\"结合事实可靠性\"等角度间接支持 RAG 降低幻觉的作用。\n\n**反驳与限定的一面（1 条反驳 + 2 条中立）**\n\n- 《Empowering Large Language Model Reasoning: Hybridizing Layered Retrieval Augmented Generation and Knowledge Graph Synthesis》(2024) 指出，即便采用 RAG 机制，在知识密集型任务中\"仍会产生幻觉和结构不连贯\"（still produces hallucinations and structural incoherence）。这说明 RAG 只能**降低**而非**消除**幻觉，且其效果在复杂任务上并不充分。\n- 《mRAG: Elucidating the Design Space of Multi-modal Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2025) 等证据则提示，RAG 的效果高度依赖检索质量、任务类型与实现方式，不能一概而论。\n\n**审慎结论**\n\nRAG 确实被广泛视为降低幻觉的有效手段，文献方向性支持这一论断；但证据同时表明：(1) 它无法完全消除幻觉，尤其在知识密集型任务中仍可能失效；(2) 效果受检索质量、架构设计等因素制约。因此更准确的表述是：**RAG 能显著降低、但不能根除大语言模型的幻觉风险**，其有效性是有条件的。若把论断理解为\"RAG 必然且完全消除幻觉\"，则证据并不支持。", "meta": {"runtime": "langgraph", "node": "reflect", "phase": "自检修正", "elapsed_ms": 794, "session_id": "t04-20260812T134352Z-run-2", "stop_reason": "completed", "tokens_in": 4859, "tokens_out": 458, "structured_answer": {"schema_version": "answer-contract/v1", "capability": "claim_verification", "status": "partially_supported", "verdict_label": "部分支持", "answer_mode": "evidence_based", "citation_compliance": "ok", "citations": [{"paper_id": "W4406838412", "title": "Empowering Large Language Model Reasoning : Hybridizing Layered Retrieval Augmented Generation and Knowledge Graph Synthesis", "year": 2024, "chunk_uid": "9d8e2b00e1c57e3ee37f521ac59ab01621b4a975", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "However, this mechanism still produces hallucinations and structural incoherence in knowledge-intensive tasks.", "stance": "CONTRADICT", "confidence": 0.8}, {"paper_id": "W4416070646", "title": "mRAG: Elucidating the Design Space of Multi-modal Retrieval-Augmented Generation", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "424741004b5b5b3b97dc8424627b6792e5c45f5f", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "However, they remain limited by static training data, susceptibility to hallucinations, and inability to verify claims against up-to-date, external evidence,", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.6}, {"paper_id": "W4405272436", "title": "ReRag: A New Architecture for Reducing the Hallucination by Retrieval- Augmented Generation", "year": 2024, "chunk_uid": "d5ab39c21c6253bb31d68dc0d60ab2b9d753c40d", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Recently, Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems (RAG) have been introduced to cope with this problem.", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.7}, {"paper_id": "2309.01431", "title": "Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation", "year": 2023, "chunk_uid": "a36067aaf8a0b7b5f7075ba84805001d3ef35f51", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a promising approach for mitigating the hallucination of large language models (LLMs).", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.8}], "uncertainty": {"category": "none", "message": "", "calibrated_rejection": false, "qualification_hints": ["该证据指出RAG仍会产生幻觉，与论断中RAG能降低幻觉风险的普遍表述不完全一致，但未完全否定其降低作用。", "该证据描述LVLMs的局限性，未直接评估RAG对幻觉的降低效果，仅提及RAG作为多模态检索增强的上下文。", "该证据表明RAG被引入以应对幻觉问题，支持论断，但未提供具体效果数据。", "该证据强调RAG解决知识截止问题，未直接提及幻觉风险，但隐含可能降低幻觉。", "该证据强调RAG结合事实可靠性，间接支持降低幻觉风险，但未明确提及幻觉。"]}, "tool_basis": ["verify_claim"], "claim": "检索增强生成能够降低大语言模型回答中的幻觉风险，并给出支持、反驳或证据不足的审慎结论。"}}}

data: [DONE]

